  "schema": "ddr-capacity-service-frozen-inputs-v1",
  "scope": "Private UI-domain composition with modeled AXI memory and ECC-control slaves. Service combines four public capacity RTL modules, private owner/register bank and v2 diagnostic mux, plus real fence/ECC monitor. Not actual MIG/PHY or physical DDR. v2 normal master mock IDs match service owner observed bus contract (ID zero). v3 checks normal memory write B ID against ID0 per owner observed-bus contract and logs actual payload on failure. v4 reports internal owner and register state on CSR failure for diagnostics only. v5 drains memory B and independent control-channel R concurrently, preserving the owner one-outstanding-per-lane contract. v6 adds raw normal-read mismatch values only for testbench diagnosis. v7 compares post-reset normal readback against retained post-BIST RAM snapshot. v8 makes Verilator sizing explicit, removes unused bench declarations, and retains success-run counters for marker reporting. v9 mock stores line indices only instead of unused address bits. v10 modeled BIST AXI checks assert full selected address bounds/alignment, consuming high/low address bits. v11 computes the mock address window via relative offset and underflow bit for strict BASE=0/upper-window lint. v12 sizes Verilator top-parameter overrides explicitly to match parameter widths. v13 tests same-edge owner rejection when platform monitor health drops after BIST done but before owner accepts completion. v14 adds raw final edge reachability diagnostics only. v15 disables the test-only one-shot corruption after its checked fault before reset/rearm completion test.",
